WEBVTT

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.632
Hi, friends. This is Kindness Detective.

00:00:12.632 --> 00:00:17.264
Sit tall in your chair. Feet flat on the floor.

00:00:17.264 --> 00:00:20.043
Hands flat on your desk. Shoulders soft.

00:00:20.043 --> 00:00:22.823
Take one slow breath with me… and let it go.

00:00:22.823 --> 00:00:30.234
Detectives notice clues. A kindness detective looks for one special kind of clue: kindness.

00:00:30.234 --> 00:00:38.571
Kindness is usually quiet. Someone shares. Someone helps. Someone waits. Someone says a gentle word.

00:00:38.571 --> 00:00:46.909
Kind moments happen all day long. Most people walk right past them. A detective stops — and notices.

00:00:46.909 --> 00:00:55.247
Let's open our first case. Think back over today, quietly. Did you see someone share something?

00:00:55.247 --> 00:01:02.658
Did you see someone help — pick something up, hold a door, make room for a friend?

00:01:02.658 --> 00:01:11.922
If you found one, keep it in your mind, like a clue in a detective's notebook. You noticed kindness. Case solved.

00:01:11.922 --> 00:01:22.113
Now the second case — and this time, the detective looks at their own day. Was there a moment when you were kind?

00:01:22.113 --> 00:01:30.450
Maybe you shared. Maybe you waited. Maybe your words were gentle, even when gentle was hard.

00:01:30.450 --> 00:01:36.009
Your kindness counts too, detective. Notice it. That clue matters.

00:01:36.009 --> 00:01:43.420
You noticed kindness around you, and kindness in you. That is Kindness Detective.

00:01:43.420 --> 00:01:53.610
Kindness was there all along. Your eyes are learning to see it. Keep them open today — there is always more to find.

00:01:53.610 --> 00:01:56.390
Hands down. One more slow breath… and let it go.

00:01:56.390 --> 00:02:00.095
Eyes open. Look around your classroom.

00:02:00.095 --> 00:02:03.801
You're ready for what's next.
